{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation evidence: RED added a workflow-expression policy test proving schedule and workflow_dispatch on refs/heads/main rendered the same concurrency group before the fix, plus a report-rendering test expecting cancelled/skipped main-health readings to be UNAVAILABLE. GREEN changes .github/workflows/test.yml to group by github.event_name + github.ref, preserving same-event/ref cancellation while separating scheduled/manual readings. scripts/main_health_report.py now renders empty/cancelled/skipped gate sets as UNAVAILABLE (neither healthy nor unhealthy). Validation: targeted tests tests/unit/test_ci_main_push_policy.py and tests/unit/test_main_health_report.py passed (54 passed); workflow parity bundle passed (93 passed); make lint, make typecheck, and full make verify with PYTEST_WORKERS=2 and GIT_CONFIG_* unset passed on retry. An earlier PYTEST_WORKERS=2 run stalled in unrelated xdist workers; a serial diagnostic run found an unrelated transient E whose isolated test passed, then was stopped to avoid excessive host load."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789008751286418001,"uuid":"dbcac88d-58ac-4f8a-b55e-fd761382a093"}